  {
   "key": "thesis",
   "title": "Thesis: leaders recover first",
   "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Write a thesis as a claim you could be wrong about, then say what would prove it wrong. Nothing here names a stock on purpose: use it as a pattern for your own."
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
       "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "The claim"
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "After a broad pullback, the stocks that held up best tend to be the first to make new highs."
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
       "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Why I think so"
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "type": "bulletList",
      "content": [
       {
        "type": "listItem",
        "content": [
         {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
           {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Buyers who held on through the pullback are the least likely to sell into a recovery."
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "type": "listItem",
        "content": [
         {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
           {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Relative strength during weakness shows where larger buyers are still active."
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "type": "listItem",
        "content": [
         {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
           {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The same pattern shows up in the base study in my research notes."
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
       "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "What would prove it wrong"
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "type": "bulletList",
      "content": [
       {
        "type": "listItem",
        "content": [
         {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
           {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The strongest stocks break below their bases while the market recovers."
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "type": "listItem",
        "content": [
         {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
           {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "New highs come first from the stocks that fell the most."
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
       "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Evidence"
